          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.087,
            0.846,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 11:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Riyaz created a math trick, which he tries out on his friend Akash."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.132,
            0.847,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Riyaz asked Akash to perform the following steps without revealing the answer to any of the intermediate steps."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.176,
            0.38,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Think of a number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.2,
            0.468,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Subtract 3 from the number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.226,
            0.425,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Multiply the result by 4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.251,
            0.399,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Add 8 to the product."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.275,
            0.425,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Reveal the final answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.3,
            0.626,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The final answer revealed by Akash was 24. Using this, Riyaz correctly figured out the starting number that Akash had thought of. Find this number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.649,
            0.175,
            0.938,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.649,
                0.175,
                0.938,
                0.373
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.382,
            0.624,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try the steps using different numbers as the"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.4,
            0.847,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "starting number. Do you see any relation between the starting number and final answer?"
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.445,
            0.847,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The answer can be found by algebraically modeling this scenario. In other words, we can form an equation using an unknown. Let the unknown starting number be x."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.513,
            0.628,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What are the expressions we get after each step?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.543,
            0.843,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.155,
                0.543,
                0.843,
                0.712
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_table_14.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Steps</td><td>Expression</td></tr><tr><td>Think of a number.</td><td>x</td></tr><tr><td>Subtract 3 from the number.</td><td>x - 3</td></tr><tr><td>Multiply the result by 4.</td><td>4 (x - 3) = 4x - 12</td></tr><tr><td>Add 8 to the product.</td><td>4x - 12 + 8 = 4x - 4</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            },
            {
              "type": "table_footnote",
              "index": 15,
              "bbox": [
                0.151,
                0.729,
                0.709,
                0.75
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Since Akash’s final answer was 24, we have the equation:"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.754,
            0.533,
            0.773
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "4x - 4 = 24"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.777,
            0.552,
            0.797
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "4(x - 1) = 24"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.423,
            0.801,
            0.757,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "x – 1 = 6 (Dividing both sides by 4)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.826,
            0.523,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, Akash thought of the number 7."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.855,
            0.846,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can you think of a simple rule that you can use to get the starting number from the final answer?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
